interventions.description:
The treatment regimen for this study is as follows:

Intravenous infusion of Oxaliplatin at a dose of 85mg/m2 for 2 hours or according to clinical practice at the research center;

Intravenous infusion of liposomal Irinotecan at a dose of 60mg/m2 for 90 minutes (±30 min);

Intravenous drip of Calcium folinate at a dose of 400mg/m2 for 30 minutes or according to clinical practice at the research center;

Intravenous infusion of 5-Fluorouracil at a dose of 2400mg/m2 (infused for 46-48 hours or according to clinical practice at the research center);

Camrelizumab at a fixed dose of 200mg, administered via intravenous drip, with each infusion lasting no less than 30 min and no more than 60 min. Administered on day 1 of every 2-week cycle (d1, q2w).

Each treatment cycle is 14 days, and all drugs are administered on day 1.

